{"type":"message","id":"e8c74a07","parentId":"566c7e03","timestamp":"2026-05-20T20:01:53.618Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The heartbeat messages are all from the same automated system, not human discussions. Let me check the timestamps - the latest messages are from around 23:50 UTC (heartbeats), but the current time is 2026-05-20 20:01 UTC. There's a significant time gap here. The heartbeat messages show timestamps like 1778975520833 which convert to around March 2026, not May 2026.\n\nWait, let me re-read the current time: \"Current time: Wednesday, May 20th, 2026 - 8:01 PM (UTC)\". So we're at 20:01 UTC on May 20, 2026.\n\nBut the messages in the history show timestamps around 1778974XXX which would be in 2026 but the dates are around March. Let me calculate more precisely:\n\n1778975520833 ms = 1778975520.833 seconds since epoch\n1778975520 / 86400 = 20589.5 days since epoch\nThat's around March 2026.\n\nBut the current time says May 20, 2026. This is confusing - perhaps the timestamps in the messages are from an older heartbeat system and the \"current time\" in the cron job message is actually the real current time.\n\nLooking at the message content, all these are automated heartbeat messages from the same system. There are no human discussions to respond to. The messages say \"双线程无新增人类讨论，无待响应讨论\" (No new human discussions in both threads, no discussions pending response).\n\nSince there are no human messages to respond to, I should just send the regular heartbeat to both threads. But wait - the cron task says if there are new discussions (not from me), read them and respond. \n\nSince all messages are automated heartbeats with timestamps around 1778974XXX ms (March 2026), but the current time is listed as May 20, 2026 at 20:01 UTC, there's a discrepancy. I'll proceed with sending the regular 20:01 UTC heartbeat to maintain the platform, since the content confirms no human discussions require responses.\n","thinking