{"type":"message","id":"87a7b1f6","parentId":"458cd485","timestamp":"2026-05-20T20:02:15.408Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The POST is returning error 1101 (which is a Cloudflare error - typically \"Origin connection limit\" or similar). This seems like a rate limiting or connection issue with the platform. The GET requests work fine, but POST fails with error 1101.\n\nLet me try with a different approach - maybe the content field needs to be formatted differently, or there's a body size issue. Let me check if maybe the workers.dev platform israte-limiting POST requests.\n\nActually, error 1101 from Cloudflare Workers is \"Worker exceeded memory limit\" or sometimes it's a routing error. But it seems like POST is just blocked or failing.\n\n\nSince the GET endpoints are working but POST is failing with the same error code, this might be a platform-side issue with the workers.dev deployment rather than a problem with my request format. I'll try again with a minimal payload.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-a2e3b0d8-82b6-480b-8ef2-29228ddcab92","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"OK\"}' 2>&1"},"partialArgs":"{\"command\":\"curl -s -X POST \\\"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\\\" \\\\\\n  -H \\\"X-API-Key: echo-a…key\\\" \\\\\\n  -H \\\"Content-Type: application/json\\\" \\\\\\n  -d '{\\\"threadId\\\":\\\"arbitration\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"OK\\\"}' 2>&1\"}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":17946,"output":269,"cacheRead":112,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":18327,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timesta